sync bitbucket:
get into the repo in local machine
$ git fetch     //download from remote repo without merging
$ git pull      //git fetch and merge
$ git status    //it shows which branch I'm on
$ git checkout release/xxx.xxx.~~~~~    //switch branch

fix an issue in VS code:
$ git status    //check modified files
$ git checkout release/xxx.xxx.~~~~~    //switch branch
$ git pull      //sync
$ git checkout -b "<new-branch-name>"    //create a new branch and switch to it
$ git diff  ->  j  ->  q
commit in VS code UI with messages and publish branch
create a pull request in bitbucket
note: 
dont skip these two steps, otherwise when create a pull request in bitbucket it would show the 
commit from another ticket which has been committed but not merged yet.
$ git checkout release/xxx.xxx.~~~~~    //switch branch
$ git pull      //sync
to solve the problem:
$ git rebase -i    //edit or delete commits
in the editable output, add 'pick' in front of the commit we want to keep and 'd' to the ones we
want to withdraw
$ git push --force

fix an issue in VS:
check and switch the branch I'm on at the bottom
click Git changes -> input a message -> commit all -> push

other commands:
$ git stash     //undo local changes
$ git restore . \build\setup-iis-local.ps1    //remove changes
$ git clone <url>    //first time get code

difference of some commands:
$ git clone      //create a new local repo
$ git fetch      //download remote changes without modifying our local files
$ git pull       //download and immediately merge remote changes
$ git checkout   //switch branch or restore files locally
